page - read a long text a screen at a time

  page /etc/services     a file
  log | page             whatever another command says

Keys: space and b page down and up, arrows move a line, enter steps,
home and end jump, q leaves the screen as it found it.

  w                      fold long lines instead of cutting them
  n                      number the lines

Folded and numbered are the same two choices `edit` offers, drawn by the
same code, so a text looks the same in both.

A line too wide for the screen ends in a dim arrow, and one scrolled
past on the left begins with one, so a cut line and a line that happens
to end there are never the same picture.

The status bar names the text, where you are in it, and whether the
tail was cut to fit memory.
